# Nothing here is required. The pages read their content live from lspd-backend when
# they open; a build keeps a copy of it for a page to show if lspd-backend does not
# answer, and `npm run dev` shows that copy. The copy is made from data/egov.db
# (create it with `npm run db:import -- --file fixtures/live-all.json`). A build with
# no data/egov.db goes on without a copy, and says so.

# Optional: make the copy from a saved response instead of the database, e.g.
#   EGOV_DATA_FILE=fixtures/live-all.json
# EGOV_DATA_FILE=

# Optional: make it from another SQLite file. The db:* commands default to this
# path (else data/egov.db), and so does a build. A copy of lspd-backend's
# data/sites/egov/site.db will do for a build, which only reads it (lspd-backend's
# schema is ahead of this checkout's, so the db:* commands and the dashboard
# refuse it). Naming a file that cannot be read fails the build; see the README.
# EGOV_DB_FILE=

# Only for a build that is NOT served by lspd-backend (the kiosk build is, so leave
# these unset for it: the page asks the host it came from, and the one bundle works on
# staging and on production).
#
# lspd-backend's origin, for the citizen lookup (the fingerprint scan in a form's
# pop-out), e.g.
#   PUBLIC_LSPD_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
# Inlined into the build, so set it before `npm run build`.
# PUBLIC_LSPD_API_URL=
#
# lspd-backend's eGov site, where the pages read their content live, e.g.
#   PUBLIC_EGOV_DATA_URL=https://gov-api.example/api/v1/websites/egov
# Its CORS settings must allow this site's origin (WEBSITE_ORIGIN there). Unset, such
# a build shows only the copy it was made with. Inlined into the build.
# PUBLIC_EGOV_DATA_URL=

# `npm run deploy` (puts the site on a server over SSH; see the README's "Deploying to a
# server"). `npm run deploy -- check staging` tests these step by step.
# The server, as ssh takes it: user@host, or a Host alias from ~/.ssh/config.
# DEPLOY_SSH_HOST=deploy@203.0.113.7
# DEPLOY_SSH_PORT=22
# DEPLOY_SSH_KEY=C:/Users/you/.ssh/id_ed25519
# The folder on the server that holds deploy-site.ps1 and the lspd-backend env files
# (prestige-nginx/deploy/windows), and a folder bundles are uploaded to (it must exist).
# Forward slashes; letters, digits, spaces and _ . ( ) - only.
# DEPLOY_REMOTE_SCRIPTS=C:/prestige-nginx/deploy/windows
# DEPLOY_REMOTE_DROP=D:/deploy-drop

# Development only (`npm run admin`, `npm run dev`): a citizen to treat as
# using the site when the browser has none, so the admin dashboard signs them
# in without the game. They still have to be on the admin list:
#   npm run admins -- add TST00001 "Mock Test Admin"
# Ignored by every build. Leave it unset anywhere real people use the dashboard.
# PUBLIC_MOCK_CITIZEN_ID=TST00001
